# Cursor Rules (legacy format — kept for older Cursor versions)
# The single source of truth is AI_CONTEXT.md at the repo root. Newer Cursor
# versions use .cursor/rules/project.mdc instead.

Follow AI_CONTEXT.md for the FoodGO project summary, stack, structure and conventions.

- Layers: routes -> one component -> repositories; only repositories write SQL.
- Restaurant scope is a required argument for restaurant-owned data.
- Don't invent UNRESOLVED business rules; leave a TODO: comment instead.
- Never hardcode secrets — use .env (gitignored).
- No new dependency without team agreement; note it in the PR.
- New features ship with tests; update docs/CHANGELOG.md when behaviour changes.
